- op: discuss  # d36b
  at: '2026-09-28T03:58:21Z'  # d36b
  by: agent  # d36b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d36b
  clock: 3  # d36b
  nonce: d36b  # d36b
  message: "Fixed in PR #1262 (60c5c7acfb). tag_io_boundaries keeps an imports-edge match only when the row is ATTRIBUTE-kind (read_not_called). imports was NOT removed from call_types: measured first, after 'from os import environ' / 'from sys import argv' the uses environ['K'] / argv[1] emit no edge, so the import is the only thing making those reads visible; a function/method row has a call edge of its own. Behavioural evidence on merged dev, the item's own repro (a file containing only import glob/getpass/socket/select/pprint/time/platform): hypergumbo io-boundaries -> 0 chains (was 4: fs_read glob.glob, host_info_read time.time and platform.platform, logging pprint.pprint); hypergumbo verify-claims {boundary: fs_read, must_not_exist: true} -> confirmed, rc 0 (was violated, rc 1). Controls pinned in test_an_import_is_not_a_call.py: from-imported os.environ / sys.argv still env_read at the file node; run(cmd) / urlopen(u) / glob.glob() reported at their call sites. Self-survey replay: 13,274 -> 13,116 tagged edges, exactly the 158 import edges. CORRECTION to the filing: taint does not read imports edges (TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES = calls, instantiates, module_attr_ref), so 'import time' never minted a taint source; the false chains were confined to io-boundaries / verify-claims boundary claims. Residual, stated in the test docstring: a function imported and used without a call (passed as a callback) now produces no chain."  # d36b
